# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Repository-root .gitignore
#
# The previous rules lived in server/.gitignore and used paths relative to the
# repo root ("server/models/", "data/Fake.csv") even though the file sat inside
# server/. Nothing matched, so the trained model and every dataset were
# committed. Rules now live here, at the root, where those paths are correct.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
.env.example

# --- Python ----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- Virtual environments --------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
server/venv/

# --- Trained model artefacts (large binaries; rebuild via train_model) ------
server/ml/models/
server/models/
models/
*.joblib
*.pkl
*.safetensors
*.pt
*.pth

# --- Datasets (large; fetched separately, see server/data/README.md) --------
#
# NOTE the trailing /* rather than /. Excluding the *directory* makes Git skip
# it entirely, and a negation can never re-include a file inside a skipped
# directory -- so "server/data/" plus "!server/data/README.md" silently drops
# the README. Ignoring the directory's *contents* keeps the negation working.
server/data/*
# Legacy top-level location, kept so a stale checkout cannot commit datasets.
# The leading slash anchors this to the repo root. Without it the pattern
# matches at any depth, and because core.ignorecase=true on Windows a bare
# "Data/" also matched "server/data/" -- which re-ignored the README below.
/Data/
# Partial/interrupted downloads (gdown writes <name><random>.part).
*.part

# Dataset payload by extension, anywhere in the tree. This is belt-and-braces
# on top of the directory rules above: no tracked .csv exists today, so nothing
# is lost. If a genuine small fixture is ever needed, re-include it explicitly
# with a negation (e.g. "!server/tests/fixtures/sample.csv").
*.csv
*.tsv
*.jsonl
*.mat

# Keep the dataset instructions tracked. This negation must come *after* every
# rule above that could match it.
!server/data/README.md

# --- Logs & temporary files ------------------------------------------------
*.log
*.tmp
*.bak

# --- Node / frontend -------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
dist/
dist-ssr/
build/
.vite/
*.local
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# --- Editors & OS ----------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
